# The owner's flag on an object report's Detail page (spec 06 §1.4, §7 Q120; GitHub issue #15;
# docs/BUILDING.md "Input scripts"), on a training game of our own in tests/input/learn-intel,
# where another empire has a colony in the home system:
# - a right-click on the flag of another empire's Planet Report opens that empire's Race Report
#   over the main window, Esc closes it; on our own colony's flag our own Race Report opens;
# - a right-click where an own colony's race pictures are opens Races On Planet, for another
#   empire's colony too;
# - in a report popup (the Colonies window's) the flag opens the Race Report as a popup over it,
#   and Esc closes that alone.
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --learn-dir=tests/input/learn-intel --training=intel --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-screen game
wait 10
key Escape
wait 5
# Another empire's colony (Prenix X): its flag, then its races.
click sector:2,7
wait-for item:report:flag
right-click item:report:flag
wait-window race-report
assert-present item:Detail in=race-report
screenshot race-report-other.png
key Escape
wait-closed race-report
right-click item:report:population
wait-window races-on-planet
key Escape
wait-closed races-on-planet
# A left-click on the flag does nothing.
click item:report:flag
wait 5
assert-no-window race-report
# Our own homeworld: our own Race Report.
click sector:home
wait 5
right-click item:report:flag
wait-window race-report
screenshot race-report-own.png
click tag:race-report:close
wait-closed race-report
# In the Colonies window's report popup: a popup over it, which Esc closes alone.
click tag:command:colonies
wait-window colonies
right-click item:"##row" in=colonies
wait-for item:report:flag in="Planet Report"
right-click item:report:flag in="Planet Report"
wait-for item:"window:##racereport"
click item:Descr
wait 3
key Escape
wait-gone item:"window:##racereport"
assert-present item:report:flag in="Planet Report"
assert-window colonies
